          "id": "weather-sticker",
          "name": "Weather sticker",
          "background": "transparent",
          "promptGuidance": "flat vector sticker illustration of a single object isolated on a fully transparent background, thick uniform deep-navy outline with rounded joins, solid flat fills in sunshine yellow, sky blue, rain blue, soft cloud grey, wind teal and warm coral, no gradients, no shading, no texture, simple geometric construction, no faces or eyes, no text",
          "subjects": "One symbol or tool that stands for the item beside it — a sun disc with rounded rays, a cumulus cloud, a rain cloud with drops, wind swirl lines, a thermometer, a rain gauge, a windsock, a weather vane, an umbrella, a puddle, a rainbow, a kite, a pinwheel, a notebook and pencil. Any subject from the user's content works drawn the same way. Never photographic, never faces, eyes or smiles on objects, never people, never snow or seasonal scenery, never text.",
          "whenToUse": "Use for symbol cargo: one oversized sticker cropping a flood card, one sticker on top of each tile in a tile grid, a sticker rail beside a list, the closing card's object. Use the sky style when the slot shows something real to look at.",
