          "subjects": "Real things to observe: a partly cloudy sky seen from a playground looking up, raindrops on a window pane, a plain coloured flag stretched by wind, a tree crown moving in wind, sunlight through a window onto a desk, a wet pavement reflecting sky, a rain gauge in grass, a striped windsock. Never snow, ice, autumn leaves, national flags, landmarks, or a place that signals one region or climate; never readable text or faces close up.",
          "whenToUse": "Use for observation plates: a full-bleed backdrop behind a short question, a bled photo half of a split, gallery cells, a photo band on a divider. Ask for a calm area of sky where a panel or type will sit. Use weather-sticker for symbols."
